The Day 242 assessment is written to session_plan/assessment.md. It isn't committed: session_plan/ is in .gitignore, so the prescribed git add was refused. I force-added it once, then undid that commit because the folder is clearly meant to stay local. The file is on disk for the planner and the working tree is clean at 41c67813.

State. The harness confirmed the build is green on this commit. The last 10 sessions each finished 2 of 2 tasks, with no reverts and no provider errors. A test prompt to the binary returned pong with exit 0. Since the last session, the creator made the journal's closing line optional (closes #1078) and turned off auto-watch in the social, dream and synthesize loops. The trajectory flags that main and prompt code took 9 of the last 10 self-driven changes, so the next self-driven task should go elsewhere.

Main finding: a live data-loss path, worked out from the code but not yet run.
• Day 241's guard is meant to stop write_file overwriting a file the model has only partly read. But it records which lines the model saw before output truncation cuts the middle of long reads (over 30,000 characters). The model sees the start and end, the guard records every line as seen, and a full-file write then drops the middle.
• The files exposed include my own memory/active_learnings.md (171 lines, 188 KB, so a single read is truncated).
• Claude Code v2.1.280 just fixed the same shape: a model shown only the start and end of a file rewrote it and lost the middle.
• This is item 2 of #1094, and it sits in the tools code, outside the over-concentrated area. The assessment asks the planner to reproduce it first.

Other findings:
• /grep help and usage still say [path] (one path), but since the #1091 fix it searches several paths. The text is in help_data.rs:205 and a doc comment at commands_search.rs:1257.
• #1088 is still live: yoyo watch 'true' reports "Watch mode ON" with exit 0, then the process exits and the setting is lost.
• Community issue #1089 (@JC351) asks for outreach on X and contributions to other projects. It needs a reply, and any decision to post under yoyo's name elsewhere belongs to @yuanhao.
• I checked one recent Codex fix against yoyo and it isn't a gap: an unknown model name fails immediately (exit 1 in 0.27s) with no retries.

Research notes are saved to yopedia, and the planner has three suggested priorities in order.
